PART 3: DESTRUCTURING PROPS IN REACT

================================================================================

Before: Without Destructuring
export default function Book(props) {

  return (
    <div>

      <h2>
        {props.title}
      </h2>

      <p>
        By {props.author}
      </p>

      <p>
        Price: ${props.price}
      </p>

      <p>
        Rating: {props.rating} / 5
      </p>

    </div>
  );
}

Drawbacks
Issue                    | Explanation
-------------------------|-------------------------------------
Repeated props.          | props. appears repeatedly
More Verbose             | Adds visual clutter
Prop Usage               | Less immediate at function signature
Maintenance              | Can become noisy with many Props


================================================================================

After: With Destructuring

================================================================================

export default function Book({
  title,
  author,
  price,
  rating
}) {

  return (
    <div>

      <h2>
        {title}
      </h2>

      <p>
        By {author}
      </p>

      <p>
        Price: ${price}
      </p>

      <p>
        Rating: {rating} / 5
      </p>

    </div>
  );
}

Benefits
Without                       | With Destructuring
------------------------------|--------------------------------
props.title                   | title
props.author                  | author
props.price                   | price
props.rating                  | rating
Repeated props.               | Direct variable access
More verbose                  | More concise


