PART 4: DESTRUCTURING PATTERNS

================================================================================

Pattern 1: Basic Destructuring
Parent
<Book
  title="Book 1"
  author="Author 1"
  price={12.99}
/>

Child
export default function Book({
  title,
  author,
  price
}) {

  return (
    <div>

      <h2>{title}</h2>

      <p>{author}</p>

      <p>${price}</p>

    </div>
  );
}

Explanation
Prop        | Local Variable
------------|----------------
title       | title
author      | author
price       | price


================================================================================

Pattern 2: Destructuring with Default Values

================================================================================

Parent
<Book
  title="Book 1"
  author="Author 1"
/>

Child
export default function Book({
  title = 'Unknown Title',
  author = 'Unknown Author',
  price = 0,
  rating = 0
}) {

  return (
    <div>

      <h2>{title}</h2>

      <p>{author}</p>

      <p>${price}</p>

      <p>
        Rating: {rating} / 5
      </p>

    </div>
  );
}

Default Values
Prop     | Default
---------|----------------
title    | Unknown Title
author   | Unknown Author
price    | 0
rating   | 0


Because the parent provides title and author but not price or rating:

Book 1
Author 1
$0
Rating: 0 / 5

Important Default-Value Rule

A destructuring default is used when the incoming value is undefined.

const {
  price = 0
} = props;

Incoming Value    | Result
------------------|--------
undefined         | 0
12.99             | 12.99
0                 | 0
null              | null


