Example 3: Destructuring with Event Handlers

================================================================================

Parent
export default function App() {

  const handleDelete = (id) => {
    console.log(
      'Deleting:',
      id
    );
  };

  return (
    <TodoItem
      id={1}
      text="Learn React"
      completed={false}
      onDelete={handleDelete}
    />
  );
}

Child
function TodoItem({
  id,
  text,
  completed,
  onDelete
}) {

  return (
    <div className="todo">

      <input
        type="checkbox"
        checked={completed}
        readOnly
      />

      <span>{text}</span>

      <button
        onClick={() =>
          onDelete(id)
        }
      >
        Delete
      </button>

    </div>
  );
}

Explanation
Prop        | Purpose
------------|-----------------------------------
id          | Todo identifier
text        | Todo text
completed   | Checkbox state
onDelete    | Parent-provided callback function


The callback can be used directly without:

props.onDelete


because it has already been destructured.

