PART 8: WITH vs WITHOUT DESTRUCTURING

================================================================================

Without Destructuring
export default function UserProfile(
  props
) {

  return (
    <div className={props.className}>

      <h1>
        {props.name}
      </h1>

      <p>
        Email: {props.email}
      </p>

      <p>
        Role: {props.role}
      </p>

      <button onClick={props.onEdit}>
        Edit
      </button>

      <button onClick={props.onDelete}>
        Delete
      </button>

    </div>
  );
}

With Destructuring
export default function UserProfile({
  className,
  name,
  email,
  role,
  onEdit,
  onDelete
}) {

  return (
    <div className={className}>

      <h1>{name}</h1>

      <p>
        Email: {email}
      </p>

      <p>
        Role: {role}
      </p>

      <button onClick={onEdit}>
        Edit
      </button>

      <button onClick={onDelete}>
        Delete
      </button>

    </div>
  );
}

Comparison
Without Destructuring       | With Destructuring
----------------------------|----------------------------------
props.className             | className
props.name                  | name
props.email                 | email
props.role                  | role
props.onEdit                | onEdit
props.onDelete              | onDelete
More repeated syntax        | More concise
Props object stays explicit | Used props visible in signature


