DESTRUCTURING QUICK REFERENCE

================================================================================

Pattern      | Example                    | Use Case
-------------|----------------------------|------------------------------
Basic        | { title, author }          | Extract specific Props
Defaults     | { title = 'Unknown' }      | Provide fallback
Renaming     | { userName: name }         | Rename local variable
Nested       | { book: { title } }        | Extract nested property
Rest         | { title, ...rest }         | Capture remaining Props
Array        | [first, second]            | Extract array items

Important: Rest vs Spread

The same ... syntax has related but different uses.

Syntax                | Meaning
----------------------|-----------------------------------
{ title, ...rest }    | Rest: collect remaining properties
<Component {...rest}> | Spread: pass properties onward


Example:

function Button({
  label,
  ...rest
}) {

  return (
    <button {...rest}>
      {label}
    </button>
  );
}


